    "result_text": "There is only one test class in the project, and it passed. The change is complete.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented tenure-based membership level 4 in `OwnerMapper.membershipLevel` (`src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/mapper/OwnerMapper.java`).\n\n**What changed:** Tenure is now a fourth level factor \u2014 the level gains 1 when the owner's tenure exceeds 365 whole days (measured as `ChronoUnit.DAYS.between(registrationDate, LocalDate.now()) > 365`), and the cap was raised from 3 to 4. A `null` `registrationDate` contributes no tenure.\n\n**Why it satisfies the spec:**\n- Reaching level 4 requires all three optional factors (email + no namesakes + tenure > 365 days), so **tenure of more than 365 days is necessary for level 4**.\n- A newly created owner has `registrationDate == today` \u2192 zero tenure \u2192 the tenure factor never fires, so a new owner (email, `namesakeCount` 0, 3-member household) lands at **level 3, not 4**, matching `AcceptanceTest.coreNewOwnerCappedAtLevel3`.\n\n**Test result:** `./mvnw -o test` \u2192 `BUILD SUCCESS`, `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0`. The audit log confirms a newly created owner is logged at `membershipLevel=3`.",
